## Complexity

Let `N` be the length of the string.

### Time Complexity

```text
O(N)
```

Each position is processed exactly once.

### Space Complexity

```text
O(N)
```

The difference array requires `O(N)` extra space.

---

## Why Greedy Works

Lexicographical order means that **earlier positions are more important than later positions**.

Therefore, when we see a `1` at position `i` and a `K`-length flip can start there, flipping it changes:

```text
1 → 0
```

This is always the best possible choice for the current position.

Once position `i` is fixed, future operations cannot improve it without potentially changing an already-fixed earlier position. So we process from left to right and make the best possible decision at every position.

---

## Key Takeaway

The main idea is:

```text
Process left → right
        ↓
If current bit is 1
        ↓
Can a K-length flip start here?
        ↓
Yes → Flip
No  → Leave it
```

The **difference array + greedy strategy** reduces the solution from `O(NK)` to **O(N)**.
